EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The proposed development, due to the intensification of
the site and the number of people proposed to be on site, would result in an
unreasonable degree of impacts with regard to traffic and parking impacts; and the applicant has failed to demonstrate that adequate provisions has been
made for waste, servicing and deliveries, would be contrary to Policies T4.F
and T7.G of The London Plan (2021) and Policies DM42.F, DM43.C, DM44 and
DM45&amp;nbsp; of the Harrow Development
Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left: 3px; text-indent: -18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;
font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;
mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, due to the loss of the
residential floorspace without reprovision,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;the maximum number of children it could
accommodate in conjunction with the retained residential use, and the lack of
supporting evidence for the need, would result in an inappropriate over
intensification of the site which would fail to comply with Policies H8.A and
S3.B of the London Plan (2021) and Policy DM46.B of the Harrow Development
Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:3.3pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;
